  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps` declares `coolantModes = true`. It reads `PARAM Coolant`.\n- An Off ask writes no coolant word.\n- A Mist, Air or Through-tool ask takes the machine's own entry of that family.\n- An ask that the machine does not state is refused by name. The warning names the operation.\n- A Flood ask is unchanged. On a machine with no coolant list, Flood posts with no coolant word.\n- The ask holds for one section. The next section starts on Flood again.\n- The flood refusal on a machine with only non-flood coolants now says \"pick another coolant for the operation (Off cuts dry)\". The old text told the user to use another post.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe Tormach mill post did not declare `coolantModes`. The engine therefore refused each non-Flood ask by name. On the Tormach 24R (no coolant list), Flood posts no coolant word. So Off was refused, but Flood gave the same G-code. The user was told to pick Flood on a machine without coolant.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew pins in `crates/post/tests/tormach_coolant.rs`:\n\n- `tormach_24r_posts_coolant_off_with_no_coolant_word`: Off and Flood on the 24R post with no warning and no M7/M8/M9.\n- `tormach_770mx_posts_each_coolant_ask_from_the_machine_list`: on the 770MX, Off writes no word, Mist writes M7/M9, Flood writes M8/M9.\n- `tormach_refuses_a_coolant_the_machine_does_not_state`: Through tool on the 770MX is refused by name and does not post M8.\n- `tormach_coolant_ask_does_not_leak_into_the_next_section`: an Off section followed by a section with no ask gives M8/M9 once.\n\nUpdated expected test: `crates/app/tests/coolant_air.rs` `an_ask_the_machine_lacks_is_refused_by_name`. It pinned the engine refusal for Tormach. Now it pins the post's own refusal of Air on a Flood/Mist machine, and M7 (no M8) for Air on a Flood/Air machine.\n\nMutation results:\n\n- Old `tormach.cps` from upstream/main: all 4 new pins fail. The failure text is \"operation F: asks off coolant, but this post script does not declare coolantModes ...\".\n- Fix without the `coolantAsk = \"flood\"` reset in `endPreamble`: `tormach_coolant_ask_does_not_leak_into_the_next_section` fails. The other 3 pass.\n- Fix restored: 4 of 4 pass.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green (81 steps, 0 failed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Heavy lanes\n\nVerified on unchanged head `1460c32b8869b43e0b9bd97e58880d6a68d20ff4`.\nBase: current `upstream/main` at `148a5c832aa811bab9cae5c7f69e0ad945ee92d4`.\nThe base stayed unchanged during the final heavy run.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: PASS, 13 steps, 0 failed, exit 0, 3.7 minutes.\n- The release build passed. The 12 selected suites executed 0 ignored tests and filtered out 92 normal tests.\n- This run executed no heavy test assertions.\n- `cargo xtask gate batch --only 'app suites: example_catalog'`: PASS, 1 step, 0 failed, exit 0, 116 seconds.\n- Catalog results: 37 passed, 4 ignored, 0 failed.\n- The worktree, golden files and catalog files stayed unchanged. No code change or push was needed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The example catalog suite passed: 37 passed, 4 ignored, 0 failed.\nNo golden, catalog, `.nc` or `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The MCP repro from the issue (`load_machine` Tormach 24R, `set_operation_coolant off`, `post`) was not run by hand. The post tests use the same machine file and post script.\n- No PathPilot control or simulator was used.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- PR #3471 touches `assets/posts/tormach.cps` (`onCircular`, `arcWord`). This PR changes other functions (coolant, `onParameter`, `startPreamble`, `endPreamble`). The PR that merges second refreshes.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/3446-tormach-coolant-off.md`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: The Tormach PathPilot mill post now reads the operation's coolant: Off posts with no coolant word (a dry Tormach 24R no longer has to pick Flood), and Mist, Air or Through tool use the machine's own code or are refused by name.\n\nFixes #3446\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
